# Citation File Format — see https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# GitHub and recent GitLab versions render a "Cite this repository" sidebar.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use vibe-view in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "vibe-view: an interactive viewer and analysis tool for QVF quantum-chemistry archives"
abstract: >
  vibe-view reads the Quantum Visualization Format (QVF) and renders
  structures, orbitals, volumetric data, band structures, densities of
  states and spectra, in a browser, a terminal, or headlessly for figure
  capture. It is a companion to vibe-qc and is usable without it: any
  code that writes a conformant QVF archive can be viewed with it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Peintinger
    given-names: Michael F.
    website: "https://vibe-qc.com/"
version: 2.17.0
date-released: 2026-09-13
url: "https://vibe-qc.com/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vibe-qc/vibe-view"
license: MPL-2.0
keywords:
  - quantum chemistry
  - visualization
  - molecular graphics
  - QVF
